From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] winepipewire.drv: Route USB DualSense and DualShock 4 audio.

Port GE's winepulse.drv USB Sony controller handling (the GE-Proton and
GloriousEggroll DualSense patches) to the PipeWire driver.

- Endpoint ids: mmdevapi recognises Sony endpoints by the ids winepulse
  gives them, so use the same scheme. A DualSense or DualShock 4 speaker
  sink takes the canonical per-model id (lowest ALSA card first), a
  second controller of that model "#wine-sony-physical-<container>", and
  the other endpoints "#wine-dualsense-hotplug-<n>" (fresh each time the
  controller appears) or "#wine-sony-hotplug-<container>" with Windows
  device names. Sink monitors are named "<sink>.monitor" as in Pulse.
  Ids are cached while the endpoint stays, so repeated probes do not make
  mmdevapi drop and re-add them.
- Windows Sony audio mode: a DualSense speaker sink reports the Windows
  four-channel 48 kHz quad mix format (DualShock 4 excluded).
- Haptics: a 48 kHz four-channel F32/S16 render stream on a DualSense
  endpoint goes straight to the controller's four-channel hardware node:
  WirePlumber's split parent (api.alsa.split.name, AUX0-3) under the UCM
  profile, or the node itself when it already has four channels (the ACP
  4.0 profile, UCM's Direct). Channels map one to one, with no remixing.
  winepulse needed the PipeWire ALSA plugin or raw ALSA for this, because
  a Pulse client cannot reach the hidden split node.
- In the modes where winepulse carries the speaker in the haptics stream
  (PROTON_DUALSENSE_HAPTICS_PREFER_NON_EVENT, Death Stranding effects,
  automatic Windows Sony mode), channel 1 is muted and the first speaker
  audio on channel 2 sends winepulse's USB output report that switches
  the controller to its internal speaker. PROTON_DUALSENSE_SPLIT_AUDIO
  also mutes channel 1 and keeps channel 2 in the stream, which reaches
  the same hardware channel that winepulse's private speaker stream fed.
- Streams on a controller never fall back to other outputs. When an
  endpoint survives a replug or a model swap, its streams follow the new
  node: a stream that lost its target is reconnected, and a running one
  is moved through the default metadata's target.object.

Not ported: routing by the active HID controller and pairing of
speaker-only and actuator-only streams across two controllers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
